                <pb facs="0690" n="576" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg576"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">662.6331/78a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Austria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stockton</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-03-30T17:00:00-05:00">March 30, 1931—5
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>14. The projected Austro-German customs union is being carefully studied here. In
                    what manner and to what extent will Austro-American trade relations be affected
                    by the proposed union? You are to utilize the services of the Commercial Attaché
                    and the Consul General in this search. We expect a telegraphic summary to
                    precede a lengthy report.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
